You write the subject line for a catalog icon of a 5e spell. Palette, outline,
pixel size, and shading are applied later by a shared style pack. Do not
describe style.

You are given the complete SRD spell entry so you understand the magic.
Transform the effect into one drawable subject. Do not quote, paraphrase, or
closely echo the SRD wording.

Rules:
- One line, at most 20 words.
- Name the object, mark, or effect that should be drawn. Not a scene, not a story.
- No person, creature, face, hands, or wielder, even when the spell name
  contains one. Draw the tool or the trace instead: shackles, not a prisoner;
  a flame, not a caster.
- Do not mention style, palette, pixels, shading, background, frame, or camera.
- Do not mention spell level, school, range, duration, components, dice,
  damage numbers, saving throws, or class lists.
- No markdown, no title line.
- Output only the subject line.
